      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_145c565905a4f1d80e71a920ca1cf832e5572b7ce8e5591efc1be942c0787a32",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: multiplying zeta by s(s-1), a pi power, and Gamma(s/2) cancels zeta's pole at one and its real trivial zeros, producing an entire xi function whose zeros are exactly the nonreal zeta zeros. Xi also satisfies xi(1-s)=xi(s). Interpretation: xi removes singular and trivial-zero data while preserving precisely the zero set relevant to RH; the reflection symmetry makes the critical line the fixed locus of the cleaned representation. Boundary: this reformulates the problem but proves no zero-free half-plane, monotonicity, or RH statement.",
